# Minimal sshd_config for a Windows PE recovery environment.
#
# Deliberately small. The stock Win32-OpenSSH file is written for an installed
# Windows with %ProgramData% expanded by its installer and a Match block that
# sends administrators' keys to a shared file; none of that applies to a RAM
# disk that exists for twenty minutes.
#
# Password authentication is on because WinPE has no user profile to put an
# authorized_keys file in that survives a reboot -- the account is created by
# startnet.cmd on each boot. The password is in startnet.cmd, in the lab
# archive, and on the screen: this is a lab recovery environment reachable
# only through a host port-forward, not something to copy onto a network.

Port 22
AddressFamily any
ListenAddress 0.0.0.0

PasswordAuthentication yes
PubkeyAuthentication yes
PermitEmptyPasswords no
StrictModes no

LogLevel DEBUG3

Subsystem sftp sftp-server.exe
